{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nFound by the `LLM-Review` bot on Gerrit change 2984 patchset 8 as three advisory findings. They were kept out of that change's scope so the cap-handler change could land without another scope expansion. All three defects are in `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` on `origin/main`.\n\n## Confirmed defects\n\n**1. `_ce_spend_today` raises `KeyError` on a no-data period.** Lines 347-357 call Cost Explorer and treat only a missing `ResultsByTime` list as zero. Line 357 then indexes `results[0][\"Total\"][\"UnblendedCost\"][\"Amount\"]`, so a nonempty period with an empty or absent `Total` raises `KeyError`. That exception is outside the `ClientError` fallback in `handler()` lines 493-505, so it escapes instead of reusing a cached Cost Explorer signal.\n\n**2. The Cost Explorer poll gate bypasses `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS` during a metered outage.** Lines 485-493 compute the due interval, but line 493 polls when `due or metered is None or metered * 5 >= THRESHOLD_USD * 4`. When CloudWatch metering is unavailable, `metered is None` is true on every five-minute Lambda tick, so the slow Cost Explorer path is forced on every tick. This contradicts the module's own comment at lines 49-54 that CE is not polled every tick.\n\n**3. `DRY_RUN` release emits a notification that contradicts the returned attachment state.** `_apply(False)` returns `[]` without touching IAM when `DRY_RUN` is true at lines 412-420. The release path still publishes `Bedrock daily cap released` at lines 562-569, and the returned `deny_attached` value re-reads live IAM at line 599. A dry-run release can therefore announce detachment while reporting the deny policy is still attached.\n\n## Resolved design decisions\n\nFor a Cost Explorer period with no `Total`, treat the reading as `0.0`, the same convention already used when `ResultsByTime` is empty at lines 354-356. The function signature is `float`, the handler already has a separate `ClientError` path for unavailable CE, and a present period with no cost data means no billed Bedrock spend for that period rather than transport failure.\n\nFor CE polling, remove the unconditional `metered is None` trigger. A metered outage must not suppress a due CE poll, but it also must not override `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS`; the retained triggers are due interval and near-threshold metered spend.\n\nFor dry-run release, do not publish `Bedrock daily cap released` when no detach happened. `_apply()` is intentionally a no-op in dry-run mode, so the authoritative observable state is the live IAM state returned by `_is_attached()`. Announcing a release without a detach is the misleading branch.\n\n## Testing seam\n\nAdd the tests to `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`. Use the existing import seam in `load_handler()` and `FakeAWS.client()` at test lines 162-245 to inject fake `boto3` clients for IAM, SSM, Cost Explorer, CloudWatch, and SNS. Extend only those fakes when a test needs to count calls or return a Cost Explorer shape not currently covered.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_ce_spend_today_empty_total_returns_zero` drives `_ce_spend_today` with `FakeCE(results_by_time=[{\"Total\": {}}])` and gets `0.0` with no `KeyError` under `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k test_ce_spend_today_empty_total_returns_zero`.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_unavailable_meter_respects_ce_min_interval` runs two handler ticks with `metered=None`, same-day cached CE state, and `ce_last_poll` inside `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS`, and observes exactly zero new `FakeCE.get_cost_and_usage` calls under `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k test_unavailable_meter_respects_ce_min_interval`.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_unavailable_meter_polls_ce_after_interval` advances `ce_last_poll` beyond `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS` while `metered=None` and observes exactly one fresh Cost Explorer call under `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k test_unavailable_meter_polls_ce_after_interval`.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_dry_run_release_does_not_publish_detach_notification` starts with all targets attached, runs the below-threshold release branch with `DRY_RUN=true`, and observes `deny_attached is True`, no IAM detach calls, and no `Bedrock daily cap released` SNS subject under `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k test_dry_run_release_does_not_publish_detach_notification`.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` exits 0 with the new tests included.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k 'ce_spend_today_empty_total_returns_zero or unavailable_meter_respects_ce_min_interval or unavailable_meter_polls_ce_after_interval or dry_run_release_does_not_publish_detach_notification'` during development, then run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`, and finally run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` before push.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe Terraform module findings from the same review stay separate. The main release guard at line 562 must not gain release-on-outage behavior; a signal outage keeps an existing deny attached."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789871457517957669,"uuid":"4dd5da81-06d5-48b4-96dc-28fc5e0ca247"}